WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:08.730
MANDIP WARAICH: Hello,
everyone, and welcome.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.490
My name is Mandip
Waraich, and I'm

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.010
the head of product
for industrial AI

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.580
in Google's cloud business.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.340
I lead a portfolio of
artificial intelligence products

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.100
that help solve some of
the most complex and hard

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.700
industrial problems
at global scale.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.140
Today I'm going to talk
about three things.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.130
First, the current
state of automation

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:36.300
and industrial efficiency and
how artificial intelligence is

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.790
revealing an entirely new
universe of possibilities.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.630
Second, Google Cloud's
approach to bringing these AI

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.050
technologies to the market.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:51.220
And third, our deploy
methodology that helps

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:57.220
achieve the impact of AI at
a global enterprise scale.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.650
Let me first begin by sharing
how we are approaching

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:04.030
our strategy to help industrial
enterprise customers transform

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.190
themselves.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:09.240
So our strategy hinges
on three pillars.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.900
First, is to provide
tools and technologies

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.820
to connect your physical assets
and workforce to the cloud.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.150
Second, is to bring both
your existing analytics

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.510
tools and new analytics
capabilities that

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:26.620
augment human decision making.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.890
And third, to drive
end to end automation

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:34.030
of key industrial processes by
embedding our differentiated AI

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:39.280
technologies into the
industrial workflows.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.410
As part of this session
I will focus only

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:44.020
on our AI capabilities.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.990
We are applying AI to help
some of the largest enterprise

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:50.110
companies transform
their businesses.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.520
We're helping the largest
airlines better plan

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.880
their schedules,
aircraft utilization,

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.870
and manage unforeseen
operational disruptions.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.710
We're helping logistic
companies achieve better fleet

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:05.770
utilization, route
planning, and maximize

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.320
the life of their assets.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.380
We're helping automotive
companies bring their vehicle

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.340
telemetry data to the cloud
and prevent component failure

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:17.680
and recalls in real time.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.780
We'll be discussing two
manufacturing focused

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.170
solutions, adaptive controls
and visual inspection,

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:26.122
in more detail in the session.

00:02:26.122 --> 00:02:27.580
Here are some of
the companies that

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.640
are trusting Google to transform
their industrial operations

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.080
and businesses using AI and
machine learning technologies.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.350
Before I get into the
details of AI technologies,

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.750
I want to take a
brief talk about where

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:44.530
we are in the broader
industrial automation evolution.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:48.220
For decades, advances in
automated controls and systems

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.190
have made industrial processes
and supply chains highly

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.390
efficient, but every subsequent
advance in efficiency

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:00.160
has demanded greater investment
while yielding leaner returns

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.280
to a point of
flattening of the curve.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.940
The staggering complexity of
the industrial environment

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:09.870
is now combined with a dynamic
and uncertain environment

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.660
like the one we're finding
ourselves right now, where

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.200
there's dramatic volatility
in market forces, disrupted

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.600
supply chains and
retail channels,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.910
uncertainty of demand, and
cost pressures to stay afloat.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.200
The current industrial
systems are turning out

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.400
too brittle and unadaptable,
narrow in their search

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.600
for efficiency gains with
years of systemized rules

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.440
and heuristics, layers
of operational buffers,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.430
and inefficiencies capped and
accrued by human expertise.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.340
These constraints make
industrial systems

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.280
a great candidate for AI machine
learning based solutions.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.320
For machine learning
based systems,

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.930
each layer of complexity
is another dimension

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.690
to explore for
hidden correlations,

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.450
allowing every aspect of
an industrial environment

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:03.310
to be analyzed minutely,
temporally, and [INAUDIBLE],,

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:07.900
individually, and holistically,
exploring new action spaces

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:12.000
and uncovering unfound
efficiency gains.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.500
These systems can adapt to
internal and external headwinds

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.100
and learn to anticipate
disruptions, allowing

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:22.470
stable autonomous operation.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.720
We'll talk through two
such examples of autonomous

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.770
controls technology, adaptive
controls and visual inspection

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:32.790
AI, both aimed at achieving
autonomous process controls

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.460
in industrial facilities.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.680
Let's first talk about
Industrial Adaptive Controls

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.980
platform that
automates and optimizes

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.220
closed loop industrial systems
like near track systems

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.720
or scaled up control
processing plants.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.200
This platform builds on
years of Google's research

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:55.430
in reinforcement learning, where
an AI agent learns directly

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:59.240
from sensory experience
and develops new knowledge

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.940
by exploring the action space
and then optimizes space

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.390
based on the most efficient
future predicted state.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:08.810
With no handcrafted rules,
a general purpose learning

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:13.500
framework, and general APIs
to take in sensory input

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.900
and produce set point
recommendations,

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.820
this platform is
capable to solve

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.915
several industrial
optimization problems.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.550
It turns out that
operating a data center

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.790
with concrete actions
and measurable rewards

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.950
is a great fit for
such a problem.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.890
Modern data centers, especially
the large ones at Google,

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.320
are complex pieces of
equipment with billions

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.590
of ways of operating them.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:41.200
For example, suppose we
have a simplified system

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.740
with 10 pieces of equipment,
each which has 10 different set

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.530
points.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:49.390
That's already over 3 million
different permutations.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.130
Keep in mind that
a real data center

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:54.160
has much more than 10
pieces of equipment.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:57.730
They interact with each
other in non-linear manners

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:01.060
while environmental conditions,
such as IT load and weather,

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.010
are constantly changing.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.410
Adaptive controls
platform has been helping

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.710
reduce energy consumption
in Google data centers

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:12.890
through direct autonomous
control of [INAUDIBLE] systems.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.590
So how does this work?

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:17.260
AI optimizes a reward function.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:21.040
This could be energy consumption
or any other function expressed

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:23.830
as a mathematical
equation of sensors,

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:28.660
while adapting to the changing
variables like building load,

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.720
and still keep meeting
operational constraints

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.310
like building comfort.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.980
For example, in the
data center scenario

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.850
the AI evaluates millions
of allowable set point

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:43.850
combinations,
predicts future states

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:47.390
of energy consumption and
operational constraints,

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:50.570
removes those that violate
equipment or safety

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.030
constraints, chooses
the set points

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:55.670
that maximizes the
objective function,

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.950
returns the
recommended set points

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:01.880
into a VMS platform to
be implemented directly

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.580
into the equipment.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.630
The generalizability
of this platform

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:08.870
allows a number of industrial
processes and facilities

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:13.280
optimization problems to be
solved using this approach.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.940
Imagine the impact that this
could have on the global energy

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:22.220
use in airports, malls,
corporate buildings,

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:24.800
waste reduction in
chemical plants,

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.550
smelters, metal
processing facilities,

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:32.520
all while achieving
higher industrial output.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.330
Another problem space where
we are applying Google's AI

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:38.600
capabilities is industrial
defect detection.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.520
Google's computer
vision capabilities

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.970
are consistently rated as
the best in the industry.

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:46.250
We've made these
vision AI capabilities

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.650
available through
our general APIs

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.350
that use pre-trained machine
learning models trained

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:55.610
on billions of images, and
through AutoML platform, where

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.220
you can bring your
own image data

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:59.900
sets to train custom
vision models.

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:03.480
Now we're taking this
one step further.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.270
We are partnering with some
of the largest manufacturers

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.910
of the world to bring
high accuracy premium

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:11.910
models for defect
detection, starting

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:15.610
with assembly inspection
and cosmetic inspection,

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:20.130
in an end to end
automated solution.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.200
We've created a dedicated
breakout session

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.730
to cover the technical
breakthroughs

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:27.840
of this technology, delivered
by one of my teammates Yinfei.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.970
Please do check it out.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.039
LG has applied our
machine learning models

00:08:33.039 --> 00:08:37.419
to achieve 99.9 accuracy for
cosmetic defect detection

00:08:37.419 --> 00:08:40.220
in their glass display panels.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:43.159
Similarly GlobalFoundries
have used our machine

00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:46.640
learning models for silicon
vapor defect detection,

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:51.560
achieving 95% accuracy across
hundreds of machine learning

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:55.010
models deployed in
their factories, which

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:59.630
makes for a good segue into
our final topic of scaling AI

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.450
at a global industrial scale.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:05.660
It's one thing running a
pilot on a small subsystem

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:08.780
in a sandbox, and it's a
completely different thing

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:12.080
transforming an entire
industrial workflow

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.630
to run autonomously using AI.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:17.810
Working across multiple
AI products, use cases,

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:19.970
and deployment
environments, we've

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:24.110
honed the approach of
deploying AI at a large scale.

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:27.830
We've come to embrace that the
real world environments are

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:33.980
highly complex, heterogeneous,
unstructured, and fragmented.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:38.920
This reality has made us design
a deploy anywhere approach

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.580
for machine learning.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:43.490
Our goal is to provide
interoperatability

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:48.560
across all computing platforms,
legacy systems and devices

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:54.890
from cloud, hybrid to edge, from
microcontrollers, CPUs, GPUs,

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:58.730
TPUs, to clusters of
servers, industrial equipment

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.280
like high speed
cameras and drones,

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:07.510
and hardware supporting MQTT
and OPC UA industrial standards.

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:10.960
In working with the largest
enterprise customers,

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.110
we have seen the challenge
of managing hundreds

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:17.470
of machine learning models
in production environment.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:20.140
Therefore we developed
managed services

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.840
that allow any kind of
machine learning workload,

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:26.530
be it a time series, an image,
or a video machine learning

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:31.360
model, to be deployed on
any kind of edge device.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.120
These services allow
you to version control,

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:36.610
monitor performance,
and retrain models

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:41.040
across a large fleet
of edge devices.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.320
You can learn more about
these deployment platforms

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:47.360
in their dedicated
breakout sessions.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.570
You can also connect with
any of our machine learning

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:52.360
specialists or contact
us through our website

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:55.360
to get started.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:58.780
Finally, I feel excited
that AI as a discipline

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:01.120
has reached a stage
where it's having

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:04.330
a direct and measurable
impact on scaling

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:07.360
our collective human output.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:09.850
Our technologies
are truly living up

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:14.170
to their promise of furthering
our progress as a society

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:18.610
and creating a more
promising future.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.320
Thank you once
again for joining,

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.320
and I hope you'll enjoy
the other next sessions.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.350
Have a great day.

